  "question": {
    "text": "Let $P$ be a variable point on a circle $C$ and $Q$ be a fixed point outside $C$. If $R$ is the midpoint of the line segment $P Q$, then locus of $R$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "a circle",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "a circle and a pair of straight lines",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "a rectangular hyperbola",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "a pair of sraight lines",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0007_8d9dcff60b1f.png\"><br>\r\nLet circle be $\\left(x-x_{1}\\right)=r \\cos \\theta$\r\n$y-y_{1}=r \\sin \\theta$\r\n$h=\\frac{a+x_{1}+r \\cos \\theta}{2}$\r\n$k=\\frac{b+y_{1}+r \\sin \\theta}{2}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow\\left(h-\\frac{\\left(a+x_{1}\\right)}{2}\\right)^{2}+\\left(k-\\frac{\\left(b+y_{1}\\right)}{2}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{r^{2}}{4}$"
  }
}